7. Phenomenological Audit

The audit remains a pre-registered qualitative component that is explicitly not a measurement of C. Operators provide free-response accounts at baseline, mid-exposure, post-exposure, and follow-up. The audit is analyzed with a pre-registered thematic analysis plan and reported alongside the quantitative results. Its purpose is to document the experiential boundary conditions under which the quantitative variables are embedded, not to test any quantitative hypothesis.

